1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:03,790
(Sheldon:)Why do we have a geology book?

2
00:00:03,953 --> 00:00:07,093
(Sheldon:)Leonard, did you throw
a children's party

3
00:00:07,256 --> 00:00:08,636
(Sheldon:)while I was in Texas?

4
00:00:09,925 --> 00:00:11,495
(Penny:)Wait. What's wrong with geology?

5
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:14,200
(Sheldon:)Let me put this in a way
you'll understand, Penny.

6
00:00:14,363 --> 00:00:16,103
(Sheldon:)You remember
how you explained to me

7
00:00:16,265 --> 00:00:18,305
(Sheldon:)that the Kardashians
aren't real celebrities?

8
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:22,207
(Sheldon:)Well, geology
is the Kardashians of science.

9
00:00:24,673 --> 00:00:27,213
(Sheldon:)Have you considered
studying standard model physics?

10
00:00:27,376 --> 00:00:29,216
(Penny:)You want me
to give up string theory

11
00:00:29,378 --> 00:00:31,328
(Sheldon:)for something
that's less advanced?

12
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,690
(Sheldon:)You know, why don't you break up
with Penny

13
00:00:32,848 --> 00:00:34,988
(Sheldon:)and start dating a brown bear.

14
00:00:36,552 --> 00:00:39,502
(Penny:)Like you could
get a brown bear.

15
00:00:39,655 --> 00:00:41,195
(Leonard:)Hey, I've got a good job.

16
00:00:41,357 --> 00:00:43,197
(Leonard:)I could buy salmon.
You don't know.

17
00:00:44,727 --> 00:00:46,567
(Amy:)Maybe you could make
your new field of study

18
00:00:46,729 --> 00:00:48,329
(Amy:)the calculation
of nuclear matrix elements.

19
00:00:48,497 --> 00:00:49,637
(Sheldon:)Oh, please.

20
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:53,039
(Sheldon:)If I wanted to take up a fad,
I'd get a tramp stamp.

21
00:00:56,839 --> 00:00:58,749
(Leonard:)What about loop quantum gravity?

22
00:00:58,908 --> 00:01:00,718
Oh, Duchess, look at me!

